{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Make statutory maternity pay 90% of wage for first 12 weeks & minimum wage after",
        "additional_details": "It is estimated that between 2023-26, SMP rose by just 12.7%, whilst the National Living Wage rose by 22%. We are concerned the gap is widening. It was estimated that the proportion of mothers returning earlier to work for financial reasons rose from 42% in 2022 to 58% in 2023. \r\n  \r\nPublic research links maternity leave under 12 weeks to greater depression, poorer maternal wellbeing & lower sensitivity to a baby\u2019s needs. Low SMP can hit low-income families hardest, forcing mothers back before they\u2019re ready. We feel Statutory Maternity Leave for 12 weeks at 90% of salary, and the National Minimum Wage for the remainder, are the absolute minimum families deserve. ",
        "background": "We believe mothers should never be forced back to work because maternity leave is unaffordable. UK SMP is among Europe\u2019s least generous, falling to around 41% of minimum wage after 6 weeks. The Government should fix this and give mothers 12 weeks of Statutory Maternity Pay at 90% of their salary. ",
